  "description": "The order a folder listing and a skill menu give two names: localeCompare(b, \"en\") reduced to its sign, so the order does not depend on the machine's language. Input: {a, b}. Expected: -1, 0 or 1 for a.localeCompare(b, \"en\"). Covers punctuation, symbols, currency, quotes, dashes, digits, letters, case, accents, expansions (æ, ß), stroke letters, ignorable controls, NEL, emoji, CJK, kana, Hangul, empty strings, and names equal after normalization. Nordic letters (å, ä, ö, æ, ø) sort with their base letters, not after z as Swedish or Danish order would. The Rust port compares with icu_collator at root with default options, which is the en order.",
